.TH RIEL 6 "2026" "riel" "Games"
.SH NAME
riel \- drive Microsoft Train Simulator routes natively on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B riel
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B riel
reads the routes, activities, rolling stock and sounds of Microsoft Train Simulator and runs them
as a native Linux program, without Wine.
.PP
There are two ways in, over the same content and the same saved selections. The graphical
launcher, which the desktop entry opens, is where most people start: choose a route, then an
activity or a path and a train, and press Play. The commands below do the same from a terminal.
The simulator itself is not on
.BR PATH .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B riel gui
Open the graphical launcher.
.TP
.B riel start
Start again with whatever was played last, from here or from the graphical launcher.
.TP
.B riel content
List the configured content folders.
.TP
.BI "riel content add " "name path"
Add a folder holding Microsoft Train Simulator content and scan it.
.TP
.BI "riel content remove " name
Remove a folder.
.TP
.B riel content refresh
Rescan every folder. Do this after adding or changing routes on disk.
.TP
.BI "riel routes [" folder ]
List routes.
.TP
.BI "riel activities " route
List a route's activities.
.TP
.BI "riel paths " route
List a route's player paths.
.TP
.BI "riel consists [" folder ]
List consists.
.TP
.BI "riel play " "route activity"
Start an activity.
.TP
.BI "riel explore " "route path consist"
Start an explore session. Accepts
.BI \-\-time " HH:MM" \fR,
.BI \-\-season " summer"
and
.BI \-\-weather " clear" \fR.
.TP
.B riel resume
Continue the last save.
.TP
.BI "riel run \-\- " arguments
Start the simulator with raw arguments, for the options this command does not wrap.
.TP
.B riel doctor
Check that this machine can run the simulator and report what is missing.
.TP
.B riel version
Print the version.
.PP
Routes, activities, paths and consists are matched on their name, case insensitively; a unique
prefix is enough.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RIEL_MSTS_PATH
Where Microsoft Train Simulator is installed. Set this when the content is somewhere the
automatic search would not look; it checks the XDG data directory, the home directory, every disk
mounted under
.I /mnt
or
.I /media
and a games folder inside each, and the Program Files folder of any Wine or Proton prefix.
.TP
.B RIEL_VULKAN
Set to 1 to run the OpenGL renderer on Vulkan through Mesa's zink driver.
.TP
.B RIEL_SIMULATOR
Path to the simulator binary, for running this command against a build directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/riel
Settings and profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/riel
Saves.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/riel/Logs
Logs. Attach these to a bug report.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/riel
Scanned content indexes. Safe to delete; they are rebuilt on the next scan.
.PP
These follow the XDG base directory specification and move with the corresponding
.BR XDG_ *_HOME
variables.
.SH NOTES
Microsoft Train Simulator content refers to its own files with inconsistent capitalisation,
which NTFS forgives and Linux file systems do not. Riel resolves those references case
insensitively, so a route copied from a Windows machine loads unchanged.
.PP
A RailDriver desk needs read access to its hidraw device. The package installs a udev rule
granting it to the
.B input
group; add yourself to that group and log back in.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/riel .
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/agustinluzardo/Open-Rails-Linux-Fork/issues
.UE .
